@startuml
actor Analyst
participant "Existing Vector Editor" as UI
participant "Next route / domain repository" as API
participant "Local PostgREST\nverified synthetic JWT" as REST
database "PostgreSQL/PostGIS" as DB
Analyst -> UI : edit local geometry (Undo/Redo)
Analyst -> UI : Simpan ke Proyek + confirm target
UI -> API : snapshot + expected layer revision + request UUID
API -> API : same-origin, token presence, bounded body, runtime validation
API -> REST : authenticated RPC (no service-role credential)
REST -> REST : verify JWT signature / role switch
REST -> DB : p4i_vector_store(save, input)
DB -> DB : active trusted profile / project edit permission
DB -> DB : lock project + idempotency key
alt duplicate request with identical fingerprint
 DB --> REST : original committed result
else stale revision / different retry payload
 DB --> REST : conflict (no writes)
else valid new transaction
 DB -> DB : PostGIS + bounded properties validation
 DB -> DB : layer + feature changes + immutable revisions + request result
 DB -> DB : COMMIT atomically (ROLLBACK on any error)
 DB --> REST : database IDs / local-ID mapping / new revision
end
REST --> API : validated result or safe error
API --> UI : committed snapshot / 409 / access denial / unavailable
UI -> UI : update binding; retain any newer local edits
note over UI,DB
Local Undo does not mutate a committed server revision.
A deliberate subsequent save creates a new revision.
External Supabase/GoTrue verification remains pending.
end note
@enduml
